    "vernacular": "Low-rise, spread-out capital rebuilt after the 1972 earthquake: one- and two-storey reinforced concrete-block houses and shops, plastered and painted in bright cream, ochre, pink and sky blue, under galvanised zinc sheet roofs (clay teja only on older colonial buildings), barred windows and walled yards. Government and institutional buildings are plain grey or cream concrete blocks of 2-4 storeys, with a few glass towers and shopping malls. Wide asphalt avenues, lake Xolotlan and Tiscapa crater, trees everywhere.",
